Subject: [PATCH] quest POI: an unloaded grid is not a bad destination

infra#2801 follow-on. Patch 0003 raised the turn-in POI cap to 5000 and dropped
the zone check so a quest could be handed in one zone away. It was correct and
it was not enough: every such POI was still discarded, silently, one filter
further down.

    float dz = std::max(GetHeight(dx, dy, MAX_HEIGHT), GetWaterLevel(dx, dy));
    if (dz == INVALID_HEIGHT || dz == VMAP_INVALID_HEIGHT_VALUE)
        continue;

`GetHeight` returns INVALID_HEIGHT for terrain that is not in memory, which is
the normal state of anywhere the bot is not standing. So the check does not
mean "this is a bad place to walk to" - for anything far enough away to be
worth a MoveFarTo, it means "I have not loaded that yet".

MEASURED, not reasoned. A temporary probe (retired in this same commit) logged
the following every tick for an hour, for a character holding a COMPLETE quest:

    [MFT] Grug: POI reject: quest=5 BAD-HEIGHT dz=-100000.0 at (-10499,-1158) dist=1905
    [MFT] Grug: POI LOOKUP FAILED quest=5 (toComplete) - every candidate rejected

dz = -100000 is INVALID_HEIGHT. The distance passed the 5000 cap and the zone
check no longer exists, so this height test was the only thing left rejecting
it. With the candidate list empty the lookup returns false, DoCompletedQuest
calls ChangeToIdle, and the module re-picks the same quest twenty seconds
later. The character oscillated inside a 40-yard box, 1900 yards from a
turn-in it had already earned, indefinitely.

WHY FORGIVING IT IS SAFE

  * Nothing downstream wants this z. POIInfo carries x and y only
    (NewRpgBaseAction.h) - dz is computed, tested, and thrown away.
  * MoveFarTo routes through PathGenerator, which resolves its own endpoint and
    already recovers from a wedged path by teleporting after five failed
    attempts. It does not need an accurate destination z to begin.
  * The POI is recomputed as the bot closes. By the time the grid is loaded the
    real height is used, so the provisional value only ever covers the approach.

WHAT IS NOT FORGIVEN: a grid that IS loaded and still reports an invalid
height. That is a genuinely bad location and is rejected exactly as before.
`Map::IsGridLoaded(float, float)` (Map.h:213) is the discriminator, and it is
public and phase-independent.

The identical test in DoCompletedQuest is treated the same way, because it is
the "double check" of a value the lookup deliberately no longer treats as
fatal - leaving it would reinstate the wedge one line later.

WHAT WOULD LET THIS PATCH BE DELETED: upstream distinguishing "unknown height"
from "invalid height" at either site, or POIInfo carrying a z that is resolved
lazily.

NUMBERED 0010, NOT 0008: 0008-bad-equip-is-a-greed-not-a-need landed on main
while this was being investigated, and 0009 is the probe this commit retires.
Two temp patches previously collided on 0008; this avoids a third.

